<title>GREECE: Greek CPI inflation falls to 6.0pct y/y in March.</title>
<headline>Greek CPI inflation falls to 6.0pct y/y in March.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek consumer price inflation fell to 6.0 percent year-on-year in March from 6.6 percent in February, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said in a statement.</p>
<p>Average CPI inflation stood at 7.7 percent in the year through March 1997, compared to 8.5 percent in the same period a year earlier, it said.</p>
<p>    Consumer Price Index    March 97   February 97   March 96</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		2.2%	-0.4%	   2.7%</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		  6.0%	 6.6%	   8.8%</p>
<p>    Index (1994=100)	   123.4	 120.7	116.6</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
